sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant P as Producer
    participant F as Dispatcher Function
    participant EV as EVENTS live
    participant AU as EVENTSAUDIT
    participant NS as Notification Service

    Note over F,NS: Scenario 1 - Success (2xx)
    F->>EV: claim Pending (READPAST)
    F->>NS: POST event
    NS-->>F: 202 Accepted
    F->>AU: move row to EVENTSAUDIT

    Note over F,NS: Scenario 2 - Notification Service down
    F->>NS: POST event
    NS--xF: error (repeated failures)
    Note over F: breaker OPENS, leave row Pending, drains later

    Note over F,EV: Scenario 3 - Database (SQL) down
    F->>EV: claim Pending
    EV--xF: connection error or timeout
    Note over F,EV: abort run, rows stay Pending, next trigger retries

    Note over F,NS: Scenario 4 - Transient failure, then retry
    F->>NS: POST event
    NS--xF: timeout / 5xx / 429
    F->>EV: Status Retry, RetryCount + 1, backoff delay

    Note over F,NS: Scenario 5 - Permanent failure (4xx), then Failed
    F->>NS: POST event
    NS--xF: 4xx error
    F->>EV: mark row Failed (Status 9) in place

    Note over P,NS: Scenario 6 - Duplicate suppressed (idempotent)
    P->>EV: INSERT event (no business-key index, so producers avoid logical dupes)
    F->>NS: re-POST same row after a crash (same EventId)
    NS-->>F: suppressed before delivery, one message

    Note over F,EV: Scenario 7 - Failed-row replay (operator)
    EV->>EV: operator resets Failed row to Pending in place
    Note over F,EV: next run re-claims and re-sends, idempotency key prevents double delivery
